=== TASK 1: cross-line dynamic range (protein vs RNA) ===
Genes with >= 10 paired lines: 8035 (of 8358 shared); fully n-matched at 30 lines: 6812

Median per-gene cross-line spread (log2 units) [n-matched, complete-30 subset]:
  IQR   : RNA 1.11  vs  protein 0.34   (protein/RNA median ratio = 0.30)  <- PRIMARY (less sensitive to isolated extremes)
  SD    : RNA 0.85  vs  protein 0.27   (protein/RNA median ratio = 0.32)  <- PRIMARY (less sensitive to isolated extremes)
  RANGE : RNA 3.40  vs  protein 1.16   (protein/RNA median ratio = 0.34)  <- SECONDARY, FLOOR-SENSITIVE

Full >=10-line set: median IQR ratio 0.30; 97.8% of genes have protein IQR < RNA IQR

FLOOR CHECK - genes split by whether any paired line has RNA == 0 (log2(TPM+1) floor):
 rna_has_zero n_genes median_range_ratio median_iqr_ratio median_sd_ratio
        FALSE    7510               0.34            0.299           0.321
         TRUE     525               0.37            0.274           0.303
 median_rna_range median_rna_iqr
            3.386          1.119
            6.348          1.976
  6.5% of genes have >=1 zero-RNA line, and for those the median RNA RANGE is inflated
  3.39 -> 6.35 log2 by the floor. But the protein/RNA RATIO barely moves (range ratio
  0.34 -> 0.37; IQR ratio 0.30 -> 0.27), because the floor-touched genes are also the
  more variable ones. IQR and SD reduce sensitivity to isolated extremes but can
  still depend on abundance and the log(TPM+1) transformation. These are observed
  cross-assay spread ratios, not calibrated TMT compression factors or correlation ceilings.

Exemplars - the MSLN 'protein 1.8 vs RNA 9.3' comparison is the floor-sensitive one:
