  All paired genes: observed cross-line SD is 1.5-1.9x the per-measurement technical SD.
  Under a homoscedastic independent-error approximation, bridge variability corresponds to
  27-44% of the variance of a typical protein's observed cross-line measurements.
  ADC targets, own technical estimate (n = 32 differences): 5%.
  This is a variance-ratio diagnostic, not an ICC. Section 4c drops the homoscedasticity
  assumption by matching the technical estimate to the observed spread within abundance deciles.

